,"conf":0.9844},{"box":[237.4,439.6,537.6,449.7],"text":"October 2019 and OMB Memorandum M-20-06 (section 31.3)]","conf":0.9775},{"box":[222.4,466.9,689.9,477.2],"text":"• Removes the prohibition on effectuating recurring discretionary changes in mandatory programs;","conf":0.9795},{"box":[237.4,481.4,652.3,491.5],"text":"|\"CHIMPs”) on an apportionment during a continuing resolution to make Circular A-Ili","conf":0.9581},{"box":[237.4,495.8,569.5,505.8],"text":"iconsistent with guidance in OMB CR Bulletin 19-04 (section 120.60);","conf":0.9717},{"box":[223.2,524.0,665.6,534.7],"text":"• Updates the Federal Sustainability Appendix to be consistent with Executive Order 13834.)","conf":0.9676},{"box":[237.3,538.5,678.7,549.2],"text":"[Efficient Federal Operations,” which was released in May 2018 to direct Federal agencies to]","conf":0.9752},{"box":[237.3,553.3,658.0,563.8],"text":"meet statutory requirements in a manner that increases elficiency, optimizes performance)","conf":0.9778},{"box":[239.2,567.9,684.3,578.2],"text":"eliminates unnecessary use of resources, and protects the environment (Appendix 10 of Capital","conf":0.9861},{"box":[239.2,581.8,345.7,592.1],"text":"Programming Guide).]","conf":0.9818},{"box":[203.4,615.3,517.0,626.0],"text":"[The updated Circular is available at the following internet address:","conf":0.9805},{"box":[237.3,647.6,597.8,658.3],"text":"|https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/a1I_web_toc.pdf)","conf":0.9632}],"blocks":[{"label":"Section-Header","bbox":[329.8,154.0,567.4,188.4],"text":"EXECUTIVE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT\nOFFICE OF MANAGEMENT AND BUDGET\n(WASHINGTON, D.C. 20503"},{"label":"Text","bbox":[401.2,218.1,496.0,226.9],"text":"December 18, 2019)"},{"label":"Section-Header","bbox":[203.7,275.2,516.6,283.7],"text":"MEMORANDUM FOR USERS OF OMB CIRCULAR NO. A-1I"},{"label":"Text","bbox":[201.7,302.7,548.7,337.8],"text":"FROME\nHee Jun\n[Chief, Budget Concepts Branch]\nSUBJECT: | Revisions to OMB Circular No. A-11 dated June 28, 2019)"},{"label":"Text","bbox":[203.5,356.5,686.1,392.7],"text":"We have updated the electronic version of OMB Circular No. A-11 to reflect some technical revisions]\n[The revised guidance:]"},{"label":"List-Group","bbox":[222.2,410.0,689.9,592.1],"text":"• Adds a reference to Executive Order 13893, “Increasing Government Accountability for]\nAdministrative Actions by Reinvigorating Administrative PAYGO,” which was released in]\nOctober 2019 and OMB Memorandum M-20-06 (section 31.3)]\n• Removes the prohibition on effectuating recurring discretionary changes in mandatory programs;\n|\"CHIMPs”) on an apportionment during a continuing resolution to make Circular A-Ili\niconsistent with guidance in OMB CR Bulletin 19-04 (section 120.60);\n• Updates the Federal Sustainability Appendix to be consistent with Executive Order 13834.)\n[Efficient Federal Operations,” which was released in May 2018 to direct Federal agencies to]\nmeet statutory requirements in a manner that increases elficiency, optimizes performance)\neliminates unnecessary use of resources, and protects the environment (Appendix 10 of Capital\nProgramming Guide).]"},{"label":"List-Group","bbox":[203.4,615.3,517.0,626.0],"text":"[The updated Circular is available at the following internet address:"},{"label":"List-Group","bbox":[237.3,647.6,597.8,658.3],"text":"|https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/a1I_web_toc.pdf)"}],"markdown":"## EXECUTIVE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT OFFICE OF MANAGEMENT AND BUDGET (WASHINGTON, D.C. 20503\n\nDecember 18, 2019)\n\n## MEMORANDUM FOR USERS OF OMB CIRCULAR NO. A-1I\n\nFROME Hee Jun [Chief, Budget Concepts Branch] SUBJECT: | Revisions to OMB Circular No. A-11 dated June 28, 2019)\n\nWe have updated the electronic version of OMB Circular No. A-11 to reflect some technical revisions] [The revised guidance:]\n\n• Adds a reference to Executive Order 13893, “Increasing Government Accountability for] Administrative Actions by Reinvigorating Administrative PAYGO,” which was released in] October 2019 and OMB Memorandum M-20-06 (section 31.3)]\n• Removes the prohibition on effectuating recurring discretionary changes in mandatory programs; |\"CHIMPs”) on an apportionment during a continuing resolution to make Circular A-Ili iconsistent with guidance in OMB CR Bulletin 19-04 (section 120.60);\n• Updates the Federal Sustainability Appendix to be consistent with Executive Order 13834.) [Efficient Federal Operations,” which was released in May 2018 to direct Federal agencies to] meet statutory requirements in a manner that increases elficiency, optimizes performance) eliminates unnecessary use of resources, and protects the environment (Appendix 10 of Capital Programming Guide).]\n\n[The updated Circular is available at the following internet address:\n\n|https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/06/a1I_web_toc.pdf)"}